#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:4
msgid "s390 Secure IPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:6
msgid ""
"Secure IPL (a.k.a. secure boot) enables s390-ccw virtual machines to "
"leverage qcrypto libraries and z/Architecture emulation to verify the "
"integrity of signed kernels. The qcrypto libraries are used to perform "
"certificate validation and signature-verification, whereas the z/"
"Architecture emulation is used to ensure secure IPL data has not been "
"tampered with, convey data between QEMU and guest code, and set up the "
"relevant secure IPL data structures with verification results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:14
msgid ""
"To find out more about using this feature, see :doc:`documentation </system/"
"s390x/secure-ipl>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:17
msgid ""
"Note that \"guest code\" will refer to the s390-ccw BIOS unless stated "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:20
msgid ""
"Both QEMU and guest code work in cooperation to perform secure IPL. The "
"Secure Code Loading Attributes Facility (SCLAF) is used to check the Secure "
"Code Loading Attribute Block (SCLAB) and ensure that secure IPL data has not "
"been tampered with. DIAGNOSE 'X'320' is invoked by guest code to query the "
"certificate store info and retrieve specific certificates from QEMU. "
"DIAGNOSE 'X'508' is used by guest code to leverage qcrypto libraries to "
"perform signature-verification in QEMU. Lastly, guest code generates and "
"appends an IPL Information Report Block (IIRB) at the end of the IPL "
"Parameter Block (IPLB), which is used by the kernel to store signed and "
"verified entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:31
msgid "The logical steps are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:33
msgid ""
"guest code reads data payload from disk (e.g. stage3 boot loader, kernel)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:34
msgid "guest code checks the validity of the SCLAB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:35
msgid "guest code invokes DIAG 508 subcode 1 and provides the payload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:36
msgid ""
"QEMU handles DIAG 508 request by reading the payload and retrieving the "
"certificate store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:38
msgid ""
"QEMU DIAG 508 utilizes handler qcrypto libraries to perform signature-"
"verification on the payload, attempting with each cert in the store (until "
"success or exhausted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:41
msgid "QEMU DIAG 508 returns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:43
msgid "success: index of cert used to verify payload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:44
msgid "failure: error code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:46
msgid "guest code is expected to respond to this operation by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:48
msgid "success: retrieves cert from store via DIAG 320 using returned index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:49
msgid ""
"failure: reports with warning (audit mode), aborts with error (secure mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:51
msgid "guest code appends IIRB at the end of the IPLB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:52
msgid "guest code kicks off IPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:54
msgid ""
"More information regarding the respective DIAGNOSE commands and IPL data "
"structures are outlined within this document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:59
msgid "s390 Certificate Store and Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:62
msgid "s390 Certificate Store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:64
msgid ""
"A certificate store is implemented for s390-ccw guests to retain within "
"memory all certificates provided by the user via the command-line, which are "
"expected to be stored somewhere on the host's file system. The store will "
"keep track of the number of certificates, their respective size, and a "
"summation of the sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:70
msgid ""
"Each certificate is stored in an S390IPLCertificate struct, which has a name "
"(converted to EBCDIC), size fields of PEM and DER data, and the raw PEM "
"Base64 data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:74
msgid ""
"Note: A maximum of 64 certificates are allowed to be stored in the "
"certificate store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:78
msgid "DIAGNOSE function code 'X'320' - Certificate Store Facility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:80
msgid ""
"DIAGNOSE 'X'320' is used to provide support for guest code to directly query "
"the s390 certificate store. Guest code may be the s390-ccw BIOS or the guest "
"kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:84
#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:140
msgid "Subcode 0 - query installed subcodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:85
msgid ""
"Returns a 256-bit installed subcodes mask (ISM) stored in the installed "
"subcodes block (ISB). This mask indicates which subcodes are currently "
"installed and available for use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:89
msgid "Subcode 1 - query verification certificate storage information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:90
msgid ""
"Provides the information required to determine the amount of memory needed "
"to store one or more verification-certificates (VCs) from the certificate "
"store (CS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:94
msgid ""
"Upon successful completion, this subcode returns various storage size values "
"for verification-certificate blocks (VCBs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:97
msgid ""
"The output is returned in the verification-certificate-storage-size block "
"(VCSSB). A VCSSB length of 4 indicates that no certificates are available in "
"the CS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:101
msgid "Subcode 2 - store verification certificates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:102
msgid "Provides VCs that are in the certificate store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:104
msgid ""
"The output is provided in a VCB, which includes a common header followed by "
"zero or more verification-certificate entries (VCEs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:107
msgid ""
"The instruction expects the cert store to maintain an origin of 1 for the "
"index (i.e. a retrieval of the first certificate in the store should be "
"denoted by setting first-VC to 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:111
msgid ""
"The first-VC and last-VC fields of the VCB specify the index range of VCs to "
"be stored in the VCB. Certs are stored sequentially, starting with first-VC "
"index. As each cert is stored, a \"stored count\" is incremented. If there "
"is not enough space to store all certs requested by the index range, a "
"\"remaining count\" will be recorded and no more certificates will be stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:118
msgid ""
"Each VCE contains a header followed by information extracted from a "
"certificate within the certificate store. The information includes: key-id, "
"hash, and certificate data. This information is stored contiguously in a VCE "
"(with zero-padding). Following the header, the key-id is immediately stored. "
"The hash and certificate data follow and may be accessed via the respective "
"offset fields stored in the VCE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:127
msgid "Secure IPL Data Structures, Facilities, and Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:130
msgid "DIAGNOSE function code 'X'508' - IPL extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:132
msgid ""
"DIAGNOSE 'X'508' is reserved for guest use in order to facilitate "
"communication of additional IPL operations that cannot be handled by guest "
"code, such as signature verification for secure IPL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:136
msgid ""
"If the function code specifies 0x508, IPL extension functions are performed. "
"These functions are meant to provide extended functionality for s390 guest "
"boot that requires assistance from QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:141
msgid "Returns a 64-bit mask indicating which subcodes are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:143
msgid "Subcode 1 - perform signature verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:144
msgid ""
"Perform signature-verification on a signed component, using certificates "
"from the certificate store and leveraging qcrypto libraries to perform this "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:148
msgid "Note: verification of initrd is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:150
msgid ""
"A return code of 1 indicates success, and the index and length of the "
"corresponding certificate will be set in the Diag508SigVerifBlock. The "
"following values indicate failure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:154
msgid "``0x0102``: no certificates are available in the store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:155
msgid "``0x0202``: component data is invalid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:156
msgid "``0x0302``: PKCS#7 format signature is invalid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:157
msgid "``0x0402``: signature-verification failed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:158
msgid "``0x0502``: length of Diag508SigVerifBlock is invalid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:161
msgid "IPL Information Report Block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:163
msgid ""
"The IPL Parameter Block (IPLB), utilized for IPL operation, is extended with "
"an IPL Information Report Block (IIRB), which contains the results from "
"secure IPL operations such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:167
msgid "component data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:168
msgid "verification results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:169
msgid "certificate data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:171
msgid ""
"During early boot, the guest kernel reserves the memory region containing "
"the IIRB. This preserves the data while the guest kernel is operating and "
"during re-IPL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:175
msgid "The guest kernel uses the contents in the IIRB for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:177
msgid "Boot logging: reports which components were loaded and verified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:178
msgid ""
"kexec operations: builds the next kernel’s IPL report from the existing one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:179
msgid "Keying: installs IPL certificates into the platform trusted keyring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:182
msgid "Secure Code Loading Attributes Facility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:184
msgid ""
"The Secure Code Loading Attributes Facility (SCLAF) enhances system security "
"during the IPL by enforcing additional verification rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:187
msgid ""
"When SCLAF is available, its behavior depends on the IPL mode. It introduces "
"verification of both signed and unsigned components to help ensure that only "
"authorized code is loaded during the IPL process. Any errors detected by "
"SCLAF are reported in the IIRB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:192
msgid ""
"Unsigned components are restricted to load addresses at or above absolute "
"storage address ``0x2000``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/s390x-secure-ipl.rst:195
msgid ""
"Signed components must include a Secure Code Loading Attribute Block "
"(SCLAB), which is appended at the very end of the component. The SCLAB "
"defines security attributes for handling the signed code."
msgstr ""
